# ===========================================================================
# ESI_2024 .gitignore
#
# Whitelist orientation: git the code (R, Py, Rmd, md) and the aggregated
# summary CSVs under manuscript_assets/. Everything else — individual-level
# data, rendered deliverables, caches, archived directories — stays local.
#
# INDIVIDUAL-LEVEL SUBJECT DATA MUST NEVER BE COMMITTED.
# Patterns below block the specific COPDGene extract and any file whose
# name hints at raw subject data.
# ===========================================================================

# ---- Individual-level subject data — NEVER COMMIT --------------------------
# Every CSV at the repository root is treated as participant-level data and is
# excluded. Analysis outputs are written to manuscript_assets/ and are tracked
# there, so this rule costs nothing and fails safe for any new data file that
# lands at the root.
/*.csv
copdgene_raw*
raw_data/
data/raw/

# Site-local input locations (see config_paths.R.example). Deliberately not
# committed.
config_paths*.R

# ---- Per-run stamps, not results -------------------------------------------
# The reproduction check is `git status --porcelain manuscript_assets` coming
# back clean after a re-run on another machine. These two legitimately differ
# per run and per site, so tracking them would put permanent noise into that
# signal and make it useless.
#
# PROVENANCE.txt records the md5 of the analysis source and the wall-clock time
# of the run that wrote the artifact set beside it. It must describe the run
# that produced THOSE artifacts, so each machine writes its own.
#
# VERIFICATION.csv is the output of verify.R, whose PRV-02 and PRO-07 rows
# differ by site by design.
manuscript_assets/PROVENANCE.txt
manuscript_assets/VERIFICATION.csv

# ---- Cached R objects (large, regeneratable) -------------------------------
*.rds
*.RData
*.rda
manuscript_assets/_cache/

# ---- Python caches ---------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/

# ---- macOS / OS clutter ----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Word / Office lock files ----------------------------------------------
~$*
.~lock.*

# ---- Rendered deliverables (regenerable from code) -------------------------
*.docx
# ...except the two live manuscript documents. These are NOT regenerable: the
# .docx is the source of truth for the manuscript (build_manuscript.py is
# retired and its prose .md sources were deleted), so without history an
# overwrite is unrecoverable. Superseded drafts under manuscript/Old/ stay
# ignored. Both are excluded from the Changit snapshot, which is built from an
# explicit file manifest, not from what git tracks.
!manuscript/ESI manuscript draft v13 2026.8.26_PJC.docx
!manuscript/ESI manuscript supplement v13 2026.8.26_PJC.docx
*.doc
*.pptx
*.ppt
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.html
*.epub

# ---- Rendered figures at project root (build artifacts) --------------------
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.tif
/*.tiff
/*.svg
/*.eps
IMG_*.jpg

# ---- Historical / archival directories -------------------------------------
OLD/
Old/
old/
TEMP/
Temp/
tmp/
background/
# NOTE: do NOT re-add a bare 'FIGURES/' rule here. This filesystem is
# case-insensitive and core.ignorecase=true, so 'FIGURES/' also matches the
# live lowercase figures/ directory and silently excluded ALL figure source
# code from the repo. The legacy artefacts under figures/OLD/ are already
# covered by the OLD/ rule above.

# ---- Build logs / one-off outputs ------------------------------------------
build_log_*.txt
*.log

# ---- Backup files ----------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.orig
*.tmp
*~

# ---- Editor / IDE ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
*.swp
*.swo
*.OLD

# Rendered response report (regenerate with render_bhatt_response.R)
bhatt_response.html
